# THE LITTLE LANTERN
# A tiny two-choice fairytale. A complete first game can be this small.

@scene first_light
background sunrise
show pip cheerful at center
"At the far end of a quiet valley, a little fox named Pip carried a lantern no bigger than an apple."
"Every evening, Pip lit it for anyone who had lost the path home."
pip: "Oh! A traveler. Would you like to help me?"
* "Hold the lantern while Pip opens the gate." -> hold_light
* "Walk beside Pip and watch the stars." -> walk_together

@scene hold_light
pip: "Thank you. Even a little light feels brighter in two hands."
"The old wooden gate opened, and the lantern sent warm circles over the grass."
jump goodnight

@scene walk_together
pip: "I like this way best. The stars can guide both of us."
"Together they followed the silver path until the sleepy valley appeared below."
jump goodnight

@scene goodnight
pip: "There we are. Everyone is home."
hide pip
"The lantern went dark, but the kindness it had carried did not."
"The End."
